# Mandalon
SvelteKit remake of [mandalon.se](https://mandalon.se). B2B site for chip packaging, bonding, and consulting services.
## Stack
- **Svelte 5** with runes mode forced project-wide (`$props()`, `$derived()`, `{@render children()}`)
- **SvelteKit 2** with **Vite 5**
- **Node 18.20.8** (see `.nvmrc`)
- **Adapter:** `@sveltejs/adapter-node`
- **TypeScript** throughout (`lang="ts"` in Svelte; `.ts` for lib modules and route loaders)
- **Lint/format:** ESLint + Prettier (`npm run lint`, `npm run format`)
- **Type check:** `npm run check` (svelte-check via `tsconfig.json`)
- **Line endings:** LF only (Unix newlines) — enforced via `.gitattributes` (`* text=auto eol=lf`). Do not use CRLF (carriage return). New and edited files must end lines with `\n` only.
## Commands
```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # local development
npm run build    # production build
npm run check    # svelte-check
npm run check:build # smoke-check prerendered build output
npm run lint     # prettier + eslint
npm run format   # prettier --write (mandatory before commit)
```
## i18n and routing

- Public pages live under `src/routes/(site)/[[lang=locale]]/` — one tree, English slugs. Swedish is default (no prefix: `/packaging`); English is opt-in via `/en/…` (`/en/packaging`)
- The `locale` matcher in `src/params/locale.ts` only accepts `en`, so `/foo/about` is a 404 rather than a junk locale
- Route groups: `(site)` for public pages, `(stats)` for `/stats`, `(dev)` for `/experiment` and `/fonts` (dev only) — parentheses do not appear in URLs
- **Slugs:** `src/lib/routes.ts` is the only place URL slugs may be defined. Build hrefs with `hrefFor(pageKey, locale)`. Do not hardcode path strings for in-site links. Retired Swedish slugs live in `retiredSwedishSlugs` and 301 via `legacy-redirects.ts`
- Content: per-page modules in `src/lib/content/pages/*.ts` (both locales adjacent in each file); `src/lib/content/site.ts` assembles `siteContent`. The `[[lang=locale]]` layout passes `data.content` to pages
- Content shapes live in `src/lib/content/types.ts`
- One page file per page — no locale wrappers. Locale comes from `params.lang` in the site layout (`en` or default `sv`)
- Site chrome (`SiteChrome`, header, footer) wraps the `[[lang=locale]]` layout; unknown paths hit `[...path]` so 404s stay inside chrome. Document metadata via `PageMeta`

## Conventions

- **Content:** User-facing text lives in `src/lib/content/` — pages consume it as `data.content`; components receive content via props (never hardcoded). Shared English-only bodies (e.g. design guide article) may live in a dedicated module under `pages/`. No em dash (`—`) in that copy; see `product-design.mdc`.
- **Code comments:** Swedish or English
- **Reference page:** `(site)/[[lang=locale]]/packaging/+page.svelte` — canonical example of page structure
- **Format / lint / check:** see `quality-gates.mdc`. Do not run them during development; they belong at commit.
